__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
.venv-qa/
# Spawn-safe launcher copied from .venv by agent-takkub.bat (issue #94) —
# machine-specific (embeds the venv python path); regenerated every launch.
bin/takkub.exe
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
src/agent_takkub/_assets/
.idea/
.vscode/
projects.json
runtime/
*.log
# Local issue-store fallback (written only when gh is unavailable). With
# issues now defaulting to the agent-takkub repo, this can land at repo root.
.takkub_issues.json
# Auto-issue dedup/rate-cap state (DATA_HOME/auto_issue_dedup.json). In a dev
# checkout DATA_HOME == REPO_ROOT, so it lands at repo root — runtime state,
# per-machine, never source.
auto_issue_dedup.json

# Claude Code per-user local settings (permission allows, MCP overrides
# vary per developer machine).
.claude/settings.local.json

# Gemini CLI per-machine config (MCP servers etc.) — tool-managed, not
# cockpit source.
.gemini/

# Chrome port files and per-shard user-data-dir created by qa shard panes.
.takkub/

# Playwright MCP session artifacts (snapshots/console logs) — transient.
.playwright-mcp/

# Local eval / scratch notes — kept out of the repo on purpose.
docs/eval/

# Cockpit-managed Codex cheatsheet — auto-planted at codex pane
# spawn time, marker-tagged, never user-authored. Safe to ignore.
AGENTS.md
# Cockpit-managed Gemini cheatsheet — same pattern as AGENTS.md above.
GEMINI.md
# Review/audit docs are intentionally committed even if the filename
# happens to be `gemini.md` (case-insensitive match on Windows).
!docs/**/gemini.md
# Gemini-role stand-in prompt (claude substitute) — a real source file,
# not the auto-planted cheatsheet. Negate the case-insensitive GEMINI.md match.
!.claude/agents/gemini.md

# Scheduled-tasks lock — runtime, per-machine (created by /schedule).
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Shipped-skill discovery surface (Phase 5a, epic #309 Capability Hub) —
# real storage moved to capabilities/skills/; core.capabilities.skill_store
# .ensure_shipped_skill_surface() (re)creates a per-skill junction/symlink
# here at spawn time so claude's Skill tool still finds them from cwd.
# Runtime-generated, never source — same reasoning as .takkub/ above.
.claude/skills/*/

# Local scratch scripts / experiments — not repo source.
scratch/

# Large local media tarballs (gameplay captures etc.) — never committed.
*.tar

# VS Code extension build artifacts (built locally; no source tracked here).
vscode-extension/node_modules/
vscode-extension/out/
vscode-extension/*.vsix

# Per-pane git worktree isolation (issue #81) — DATA_HOME/worktrees. In a dev
# checkout DATA_HOME == repo root, so isolated worktrees land here; never track them.
worktrees/

# graphify knowledge-graph output (generated)
graphify-out/

# graft's externalized code-graph store (#146 follow-up) — graft_store.py.
# Lives under the user's home dir (~/.agent-takkub/graft-graphs/<instance>/),
# never under DATA_HOME/this repo — a dev-checkout regression (found
# 2026-08-05) had it default to DATA_HOME, which for a dev checkout equals
# REPO_ROOT, so the store landed INSIDE this very repo whenever agent-takkub
# was itself a configured project; that's what caused the `.ignore`
# un-ignore rule below to actually fire. Fixed in graft_store.py, but this
# pattern stays as a defensive backstop against any future regression of
# the same kind (a store nested back inside the tree) — not because it
# fires routinely anymore.
graft-graphs/

# `graft build` regenerates a `.ignore` next to whatever it just indexed, to
# re-admit its own generated output to ripgrep, WHEN the `--dir` store ends
# up nested inside the indexed target (see the graft-graphs/ comment above
# for how that happened here). Two places that pattern could land in this
# repo, neither ever hand-authored by us:
#   * src/agent_takkub/.ignore — from the original in-place pilot build; it
#     re-admits graft's 141 generated cards to ripgrep (stale line numbers,
#     doubles every grep hit), which is why we ship src/agent_takkub/.rgignore
#     instead — .rgignore outranks .ignore and graft never touches it.
#   * ./.ignore (repo root) — written back whenever the graft-graphs/ store
#     regresses to living inside the tree (see above); now a defensive
#     backstop, not an expected boot-time artifact.
# Unanchored so it covers both and any future build target — we author our
# ripgrep excludes as .rgignore, so no .ignore in this tree is ever ours.
.ignore
